{
  "esm": "2.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "weno5_eno1_blend_D1x_extrapolate_bc",
    "description": "Per-axis derivative diff2x of NCAR fire_behavior's fire_upwinding = 10 (WENO5/ENO1 with a cosine blending zone; physics/level_set_mod.F90 Calc_tend_ls case 10) on EarthSciDiscretizations' cartesian_uniform_2d grid with the linear-extrapolation halo closure. The reference code blends the PER-AXIS derivative, diff2x = mask diff2x_weno + (1 - mask) diff2x_eno, and builds both |grad psi| = sqrt(diff2x^2 + diff2y^2) and the front normal nvx = diff2x/sqrt(|grad psi|^2 + eps) from it, so a consumer that lowers its norm with ESD's rules/weno5_eno1_blend_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc must lower its bare D(u, wrt: x) with the SAME blend, not with the hard-edged fire_upwinding = 9 rule rules/weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_bc. ESD ships the blend only inside the compound norm rule; this rule is the missing per-axis sibling, written exactly as rules/weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_bc with its interior stencil swapped: the body applies ESD's shared boundary frame rules/weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_frame (ENO1 strips, guarded linear-extrapolation ghosts of Extrapol_var_at_bdys at the x walls) around ESD's stencils/weno5_eno1_blend_D1x_interior (mask = 1 for |u| <= B, 0.5 (1 + cos(pi (|u| - B)/B)) over B < |u| <= 2B, 0 beyond and in the bdy_eno1_cells wall band; B = weno_band_cells dx). Match D(u, wrt: x) at priority 10, scoped with where {u: {shape: [x, y]}} (esm-spec 9.6.1), the same pattern and priority as the fire_upwinding = 9 rule, so a component imports one or the other. Local to this repository because ESD has no per-axis blend rule. Free names (consumer scope): wind_u, wind_v, bdy_eno1_cells (>= 3), weno_band_cells, pi_blend, dx, dy. Requires NX, NY >= 7.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "discretization",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "op:D",
      "axis:x",
      "bc:extrapolate_linear",
      "fire_upwinding:10"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Munoz-Esparza, D., Kosovic, B., Jimenez, P. A., & Coen, J. L. (2018). An accurate fire-spread algorithm in the Weather Research and Forecasting model using the level-set method. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 10(4), 908-926.",
        "doi": "10.1002/2017MS001108"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), physics/level_set_mod.F90: Calc_tend_ls (case 4 and case 10, the `use eno1 near domain boundaries` band test that precedes the select case), Select_eno, Select_weno5, Extrapol_var_at_bdys. Identical in WRF phys/fire_behavior/physics/level_set_mod.F90."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_frame.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/stencils/weno5_eno1_blend_D1x_interior.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "weno5_eno1_blend_D1x_extrapolate_bc": {
      "params": [
        "u"
      ],
      "priority": 10,
      "match": {
        "op": "D",
        "args": [
          "u"
        ],
        "wrt": "x"
      },
      "where": {
        "u": {
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ]
        }
      },
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_frame",
        "bindings": {
          "u": "u",
          "interior": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "weno5_eno1_blend_D1x_interior",
            "bindings": {
              "u": "u"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
